{"Header":{"Name":"padi.test.phase1","Version":"1","Pub Date":"2026-09-11T21:46:39.562Z","Status":"Published","Owner":"Padi, Inc.","Title":"Phase 1 Exercise","Provider":"Exerciser","Consumer":"Observer","Description":"A test Profile published to exercise registration, publication and Channels on the canonical Registry (cp.cnscp.io) at the opening of Phase 1, 11 September 2026. The Provider reports its state and carries an event feed; the Consumer may leave a note. Under padi.test by design: local exercise, never intended to govern a real Connection.","Website":"https://github.com/CNSCP/registry/blob/main/REGISTRY-DESIGN.md"},"Properties":{"Provider":[{"Name":"state","Mandatory":"yes","Propagate":"yes","Default":"ready","Description":"The exerciser's state: ready, running, or done.","Sample":"running"}],"Consumer":[{"Name":"note","Mandatory":"no","Propagate":"no","Description":"A free-text note from the observer, meaningful to the one exerciser it is addressed to.","Sample":"looks fine from here"}]},"Channels":[{"Name":"events","Mode":"message","Protocol":"mqtt","Provider Role":"server","Consumer Role":"client","Description":"An ordered message channel carrying MQTT: the Provider plays the broker (server), the Consumer a client. Exists to show a Channel on a published Profile; what is published on it is the exerciser's business."}]}